\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Symmetries of graded spin fields}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{A coordinate inversion or a conjugation of coefficients can
carry a Fourier mode to a different momentum block. How does
the action on a rotation within the block change? What can the
spectrum of the centered operator say about the rotation?}

\p{The grading and the internal action also belong to the field
space. When does a conjugation exist on that space, and which
maps can exchange the two parts of a graded coupling?}

\transclude{fdip-0171}
